<topic id="GUID-2AF8B7D4-78AE-4958-90A2-A5AE30F061FD" xml:lang="en-US"> 
  <title>Package Power Information</title> 
  <body> 
	 <p> 
	 <ul id="GUID-5D7A2305-B571-4D92-8CD2-C0BA32764E41"> 
		<li id="LI_729D761D21E140FEAF2EA88CD44CC7BA">The power values given below are for IA centric workload which does not include all the feature rich power adders available in NVL (I/O connectivity scenarios). The IOE powers will depend on workload. For more details, refer to the Feature Rich section. 
		</li> 
		<li id="LI_ACA9EE3BBBF540A999D3C555B4A7E292">To know about power adder estimation for various I/O connectivity scenarios, refer to the Nova Lake H Platform Design Guide and Nova Lake-HX Platform Design Guide (#<xref href="HTTPS://CDRDV2.INTEL.COM/V1/DL/GETCONTENT/855310" format="HTTPS" scope="external">855310</xref> and #<xref href="HTTPS://CDRDV2.INTEL.COM/V1/DL/GETCONTENT/854352" format="HTTPS" scope="external">854352</xref>). System designers should consider the thermally relevant power adder of different I/O connections scenarios on processor and platform, when determining the thermal budget and associated cooling solution to preserve similar user experiences or performance. 
		</li> 
		<li id="LI_F20F183AEB524C51B6FCF2FAC72553AD">The below table shows power splits for the IA-centric workload used for sustained cooling needs considered in 
		  <xref scope="local" format="dita" href="GUID-680A8FDF-E411-4147-8343-017ACCB4FA39.dita">section 3.5</xref>. 
		</li> 
	 </ul> 
	 </p> 
