		<p> 
		  <sup>1</sup> Processor Base Power (PBP)=25W for 8C/16C 12X<sup>e</sup>/16C 4X<sup>e</sup>. 
		</p> 
		<p><sup>2</sup> Processor Base Power(PBP)=15W for 14C4X<sup>e</sup>. 
		</p> 
		<p> 
		  <sup>3</sup> Processor Base Power (PBP)=55W for HX 16C/HX 28C/HX 24C. 
		</p> 
		<p> 
		  <sup>4</sup> PL1=25W (or any power 10-45W) can be configured in BIOS for 8C. 
		</p> 
		<p><sup>5</sup> PL1=15W (or any power 10-25W) can be configured in BIOS for14C 4X<sup>e</sup>. 
		</p> 
		<p><sup>6</sup> PL1=45W (or any power 25-65W) can be configured in BIOS for 16C 12X<sup>e</sup> and 16C. 
		</p> 
		<p> 
		  <sup>7</sup> PL1=55W (or any power 35-65W) can be configured in BIOS for HX 16C. 
		</p> 
		<p><sup>8</sup> PL1=55W (or any power 35-85W) can be configured in BIOS for HX 28C &amp; HX 24C. 
		</p> 
		<p><sup>9</sup> The equations are applicable only between the range of minimum assured power/processor base power to maximum assured power. 
		</p> 
